15 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Illustration depicting a process where a microscopic image of bacteria is captured and processed by a convolutional neural network model, resulting in the identification of bacterial characteristics such as gram stain and spore formation in a CSV file, with Escherichia coli shown as the identified species.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Heatmap visualizing metadata for thirty bacterial and fungal species, with features along the x-axis such as Gram stain, shape, oxygen requirement, temperature range, biosafety level, pathogenicity, natural habitat, and motility; colors encode distinct categories, clarified in a legend at the right.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustration of a Gram-stained microscopy classification CNN architecture divided into three stages: input and preprocessing, convolution blocks, and classification. Labeled blocks depict input image handling, sequential convolutional layers with feature shapes, a flattening layer, a fully connected dense layer, and a final output layer indicating classification into 33 classes.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Two side-by-side line charts compare training and validation performance across one hundred epochs. Left chart shows training and validation accuracy rising from zero to above zero point eight. Right chart shows training and validation loss decreasing from about three point five to near zero point five.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Multi-class ROC curve chart illustrating taxonomic classification performance with true positive rate on the y-axis and false positive rate on the x-axis, featuring macro-average, micro-average, and random chance lines, alongside multiple colored ROC curves for various bacterial species, as listed in the legend on the right. An inset plot shows zoomed individual curves for each class.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Confusion matrix heatmap displaying classification performance for various bacterial and fungal species with true labels on the Y-axis, predicted labels on the X-axis, and a blue color scale indicating prediction frequency.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Nine microscope images of bacterial samples, each labeled with actual species, predicted species, and confidence level. Circular fields display various stained bacterial morphologies, purple or pink cells on pale backgrounds, used for species identification accuracy comparison.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Microscope photograph of pink-stained, round Veillonella bacteria indicating Gram-negative cocci, displayed with key characteristics below such as anaerobic metabolism, non-pathogenicity, oral cavity habitat, and non-motile nature.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
